<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nancy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nancy is a city on the Meurthe in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the historic capital of the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>. The dukes made it their residence from the 12th century, and outside its walls René II defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a> in 1477. Under Duke Stanislaus Leszczyński it gained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/place-stanislas">Place Stanislas</a>, now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>, and around 1900 it was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/art-nouveau">Art Nouveau</a>.</p></div>
